@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 160
hide footbox
title TechZone — sale creation and safe retry
actor "ADMIN / SALES" as Staff
boundary "React client" as UI
control "Express route\n+ auth guards" as API
control "sales/service.js" as Sale
control "inventory/service.js" as Stock
database "MongoDB\nreplica set" as DB
Staff -> UI : Submit sale
UI -> API : POST /api/sales\nitems, key, cookie
API -> DB : Resolve session\nand active user
DB --> API : User + role
API -> API : Check permission;\nvalidate body/key
API -> Sale : recordSale(items,\nuserId, key)
note over API, Sale
  Invalid session / permission / input returns 401 / 403 / 400.
  Matching in-flight requests share a promise; conflicting reuse returns 409.
end note
group MongoDB transaction
  Sale -> DB : Find Sale by requestId
  DB --> Sale : Existing sale or none
  alt Existing key with different actor or ordered items
    Sale -> Sale : Reject with 409
  else Existing key with matching actor and ordered items
    Sale -> Sale : Return existing sale\n(no stock writes)
  else New key
    Sale -> DB : Recheck actor; read\nactive products and stock
    Sale -> Sale : Validate stock and totals;\nbuild price snapshots
    Sale -> DB : Save Sale and items
    loop Each sale item
      Sale -> Stock : applyStockChange\n(-qty, SALE, saleId,\nuserId, session)
      Stock -> DB : Recheck actor;\nlock active product
      Stock -> DB : Guarded stock decrement;\nappend inventory event
      Stock --> Sale : Updated stock and event
    end
  end
  note over Sale, DB
    Commit only on success. Any failure aborts the whole transaction,
    including all earlier stock/history writes and the sale.
  end note
end
Sale --> API : Sale or error
API --> UI : 201 {sale} or error
UI --> Staff : Show result; refresh\ninventory after success
note over Sale, DB
  Unique requestId guards retries across processes/restarts.
  Duplicate-key recovery reads and validates the committed sale.
  Driver retries and low-level model validation are omitted.
end note
@enduml
